Figure 3: Distribution of Vannmiljø copper samples by water category and reported sampling medium, all years





Table 3 gives the cumulative proportion of samples corresponding to each combination of reported water category and medium. This allows us to make strategic decisions about which groups to prioritise conversion into our eData format. I have elected to use 90% as an arbitrary cut-off point - that is, once I have 90% coverage of water categories and sampling media (before date-based sampling), I will consider that sufficient data.


Code
# Calculate sample distribution with cumulative percentages
sample_distribution &lt;- vm_exploration_vkat_x_medium |&gt;
  arrange(desc(n_samples)) |&gt;
  mutate(
    pct_of_total = 100 * n_samples / sum(n_samples),
    cumulative_n = cumsum(n_samples),
    cumulative_pct = 100 * cumulative_n / sum(n_samples)
  ) |&gt;
  select(
    Vannkategori_Description,
    MediumID_Name,
    n_samples,
    pct_of_total,
    cumulative_n,
    cumulative_pct
  )

datatable(
  sample_distribution,
  colnames = c(
    "Water Category",
    "Medium",
    "N Samples",
    "% of Total",
    "Cumulative N",
    "Cumulative %"
  ),
  options = list(
    pageLength = 10,
    order = list(list(3, 'desc'))
  )
) |&gt;
  formatRound(columns = c("pct_of_total", "cumulative_pct"), digits = 1) |&gt;
  formatCurrency(
    columns = c("n_samples", "cumulative_n"),
    currency = "",
    digits = 0
  )




